====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|now|_|rare}} To make and repair barrels etc.
# {{lb|en|transitive|slang|obsolete}} To [[forge]] or [[imitate]] (writing).
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1872|author=Augustus Mayhew|title=Paved with Gold|page=269
|passage={{...}} though, owing to his forged signatures having been too often detected, he was declared to be "a duffer at '''coopering''' a monekur."}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|slang|obsolete}} To intentionally [[injure]] (a [[racehorse]]) to spoil its chances of winning.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1864|journal=Baily's Magazine of Sports & Pastimes|volume=8|page=110
|passage=Every design that villainy could suggest was had recourse to in the hopes of nobbling Wild Dayrell; but never being left for an hour by either his trainer or jockey, he escaped the intended ''''coopering'''', even when the lynchpins of the wheels of his van had been tampered with.}}

